# trace_studio trace: grid_load + an ABSOLUTE capture range over the load-flip
# (map-entry) tick — the RICH draw-stepping case.  Same load flow as
# grid_load_dense.jsonl, but the captures are deliberately absolute (no
# {wait}), because the full-map render happens on the load-flip tick which is
# ONE tick BEFORE the MAP_FREEROAM anchor fires — anchor+offset can't reach it.
#
# The flip frame (≈present 640 with --rng-seed) renders the whole map as ~269
# SPRITE draws (terrain tiles + objects) + ~196 GLYPH draws (HUD); stepping it
# in the viewer builds the map up tile-by-tile from the load screen.  The
# trailing frames are glyph-only HUD redraws (dirty-rect steady state).
#
# Port-only by design (absolute frames don't align port↔retail — the cross-
# engine flip-anchor is Phase 2b work); drive with `--only port`.
{"wait": "TITLE"}
